{%- comment -%}
  Continue shopping -> the headless storefront.

  Shopify's new checkout gives no setting for where "Continue shopping" on the
  thank-you page points: it always goes to the online store's root. There is no
  admin option and no Storefront API field for it (confirmed against Shopify's
  own developer forum, where the question is still open).

  So redirect the online store instead. Paste this at the very top of
  layout/theme.liquid, immediately after the opening <head> tag, in whichever
  theme the Online Store channel is publishing. Checkout, the thank-you page and
  customer accounts are not themed, so none of them are affected — only the
  storefront pages a shopper would land on, which is exactly what we want to
  hand back to the headless site.

  The path is carried across, so /products/sos-alarm on the myshopify domain
  lands on /products/sos-alarm here rather than dumping everyone on the home page.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign headless_origin = 'https://whaleora.com' -%}

{%- unless request.design_mode -%}
  <script>
    (function () {
      // Theme editor, previews and the password page must still render, or the
      // theme becomes impossible to edit.
      var search = window.location.search;
      if (search.indexOf('preview_theme_id') > -1 || search.indexOf('_ab=') > -1) return;
      if (window.location.pathname.indexOf('/password') === 0) return;
      if (window.self !== window.top) return;

      var target = {{ headless_origin | json }}
        + window.location.pathname
        + window.location.search
        + window.location.hash;
      window.location.replace(target);
    })();
  </script>
  <noscript>
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ headless_origin }}">
  </noscript>
{%- endunless -%}
